  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Icebreaker Kraken's enters-the-battlefield ability won't tap any artifacts or creatures.",
      "oracle_id": "01590ff3-34fa-47aa-b5da-f0b8c1b031c6",
      "published_at": "2021-02-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "No artifacts or creatures controlled by the player affected by Icebreaker Kraken's enters-the-battlefield ability will untap during that player's next untap step, even if they were untapped as the ability resolved or that player didn't control them at that time.",
      "oracle_id": "01590ff3-34fa-47aa-b5da-f0b8c1b031c6",
      "published_at": "2021-02-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once you announce that you're activating the last ability, no player may take actions until the ability has been paid for. Notably, opponents can't try to stop you from activating it by removing your snow lands.",
      "oracle_id": "01590ff3-34fa-47aa-b5da-f0b8c1b031c6",
      "published_at": "2021-02-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Snow is a supertype, not a card type. It has no rules meaning or function by itself, but spells and abilities may refer to it.",
      "oracle_id": "01590ff3-34fa-47aa-b5da-f0b8c1b031c6",
      "published_at": "2021-02-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Snow isn't a type of mana. If an effect says you may spend mana as though it were any type, you can't pay for {S} using mana that wasn't produced by a snow source.",
      "oracle_id": "01590ff3-34fa-47aa-b5da-f0b8c1b031c6",
      "published_at": "2021-02-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Some cards have additional effects for each {S} spent to cast them. You can cast these spells even if you don't spend any snow mana to cast them; their additional effects simply won't do anything.",
      "oracle_id": "01590ff3-34fa-47aa-b5da-f0b8c1b031c6",
      "published_at": "2021-02-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The Kaldheim set doesn't have any cards with mana costs that include {S}, but some previous sets do. If an effect says such a spell costs {1} less to cast, that reduction doesn't apply to any {S} costs. This is also true for activated abilities that include {S} in their activation costs and effects that reduce those costs.",
      "oracle_id": "01590ff3-34fa-47aa-b5da-f0b8c1b031c6",
      "published_at": "2021-02-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The {S} symbol is a generic mana symbol. It represents a cost that can be paid by one mana that was produced by a snow source. That mana can be any color or colorless.",
      "oracle_id": "01590ff3-34fa-47aa-b5da-f0b8c1b031c6",
      "published_at": "2021-02-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost you're paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions (such as that of Icebreaker Kraken). The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.",
      "oracle_id": "01590ff3-34fa-47aa-b5da-f0b8c1b031c6",
      "published_at": "2021-02-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you Donate an Aura, it stays where it is, but the targeted player now controls it.",
      "oracle_id": "049d1fb2-cce7-40e7-a633-e84cf9782d89",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Prowess of the Fair and another nontoken Elf are put into your graveyard simultaneously (by Akroma's Vengeance, for example), the other Elf will cause Prowess of the Fair's ability to trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "31324235-8a2b-4ce4-b0d4-6d947489b930",
      "published_at": "2007-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Kindred is a card type that allows noncreature cards to have creature types. For example, Echoes of Eternity is an Eldrazi (although not a creature) while on the battlefield and an Eldrazi card (although not a creature card) in zones other than the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "31324235-8a2b-4ce4-b0d4-6d947489b930",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This cards was originally printed with the \"tribal\" card type. That card type has been replaced with \"kindred\". This change does not affect the gameplay function of this card.",
      "oracle_id": "31324235-8a2b-4ce4-b0d4-6d947489b930",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "While it appears only on cards that already have other card types, kindred is a card type and will be counted by effects that refer to the number of card types among cards in a zone.",
      "oracle_id": "31324235-8a2b-4ce4-b0d4-6d947489b930",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once a player announces that they're casting a spell or activating an ability, no player may take other actions until the spell or ability has been paid for. Notably, other players can't try to tap that player's permanents to stop them from paying {T} or to stop them from producing enough mana.",
      "oracle_id": "3608f1f7-8dc5-4dd1-ae91-c830e1de9529",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Returning the Forest you control to its owner's hand is the cost to activate the ability. Once you activate the ability, no one can try to do anything to the Forest to stop you from activating the ability.",
      "oracle_id": "3ecaefc8-ead2-47a3-a7ea-b030faab65a7",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can target any creature with Quirion Ranger's ability, not just a tapped creature.",
      "oracle_id": "3ecaefc8-ead2-47a3-a7ea-b030faab65a7",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You may return any land you control with the subtype Forest. It doesn't have to be one named Forest.",
      "oracle_id": "3ecaefc8-ead2-47a3-a7ea-b030faab65a7",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.",
      "oracle_id": "60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb",
      "published_at": "2004-12-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".",
      "oracle_id": "60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb",
      "published_at": "2010-06-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Returning the Elf you control to its owner's hand is the cost to activate the ability. Once you activate the ability, no one can try to do anything to the Elf to stop you from activating the ability.",
      "oracle_id": "67a52a74-9474-4f4e-8785-6ff54078a8ca",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can target any creature with Wirewood Symbiote's ability, not just a tapped creature.",
      "oracle_id": "67a52a74-9474-4f4e-8785-6ff54078a8ca",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This has basic land types, but it isn't a basic land. Things that affect basic lands don't affect it. Things that affect basic land types do.",
      "oracle_id": "74b7fe23-5d3a-4092-8d78-7c0eba8f6f73",
      "published_at": "2008-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This has the mana abilities associated with both of its basic land types.",
      "oracle_id": "74b7fe23-5d3a-4092-8d78-7c0eba8f6f73",
      "published_at": "2008-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Ovinomancer is a legal target for its own ability. Activating that ability will cause Ovinomancer to return to its owner’s hand, so the ability will have an illegal target. It won’t resolve, and no one will create a Sheep token.",
      "oracle_id": "98026d30-a29f-4590-968f-b1b36926a275",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The two targets can have different card types. For example, you can target one artifact and one creature with Ghostly Flicker.",
      "oracle_id": "ad0070db-6454-41cb-861f-8f5b8fc2a3b8",
      "published_at": "2017-03-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The enchanted land loses its existing land types and any abilities printed on it. It now has the land type Island and has the ability to tap to produce {U}. Spreading Seas doesn't change the enchanted land's name or whether it's legendary, basic, or snow.",
      "oracle_id": "af32757c-9d3c-4f6c-a6fa-d5729a440382",
      "published_at": "2009-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a creature enters the battlefield under your control and gains haste, but then loses it before attacking, it won't be able to attack that turn. This means that you can't use one Lightning Greaves to allow two new creatures to attack in the same turn.",
      "oracle_id": "ca204b66-8d0c-431a-8d34-282f7c2d17da",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't simply unequip Equipment from a creature. If Lightning Greaves is attached to the only creature you control, you won't be able to attach other equipment to it (or target it with anything else) until you have another creature to which you can attach Lightning Greaves.",
      "oracle_id": "ca204b66-8d0c-431a-8d34-282f7c2d17da",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like indestructible and the ability granted by Belligerent Sliver, having more than one instance of the ability doesn’t provide any additional benefit.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Damage dealt to a Sliver with indestructible is still marked on that creature. If it has lethal damage marked on it and it loses indestructible (perhaps because Sliver Hivelord leaves the battlefield), it will be destroyed.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you change the creature type of a Sliver you control so it’s no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures you control.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Slivers in this set affect only Sliver creatures you control. They don’t grant bonuses to your opponents’ Slivers. This is the same way Slivers from the Magic 2014 core set worked, while Slivers in earlier sets granted bonuses to all Slivers.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
